Summary: Start a 64-bit program at its entry point when its random base was already taken
Category: system
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: written for wine-mac-builds
Source: none published
Upstream: no (WineHQ master unchanged, checked 2026-11-17)
Why: since Wine 11, the server gives each 64-bit exe a random base in
 0x7ff600000000-0x7ff800000000, as Windows does. When that range is
 already in use in the new process, map_image_view() maps the exe
 somewhere else (often 0x10000), but the image information keeps the
 assigned address in map_addr, and virtual_fill_image_information()
 computes TransferAddress from map_addr. The main thread then starts at
 the entry point of the assigned address, where nothing is mapped, and
 the process dies with a page fault on execute before any of its code
 runs. On macOS that range also holds host mappings, Rosetta's among
 them, so this happens about once in several hundred processes. After
 mapping, set map_addr to where the image really is. 10.0 has no random
 exe bases.
 Seen in Second Chance's Nancy Drew integration run (11.22-build4):
 start.exe crashed at base+0x36a0 (its entry point) before Shadow at the
 Water's Edge and Sea of Darkness started; explorer.exe at base+0xefa0
 in a build step.
Evidence: tests/regress/exe-base-taken.c takes the child's assigned base
 on the host side before the child maps its exe: the child crashes at
 base + entry every time without this patch.
Applies to: wine 11.22 (macfixes, after 0058)
Status: 2026-11-17: not yet built.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index b608594..a0bc146 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3194,6 +3194,12 @@ static NTSTATUS virtual_map_image( HANDLE mapping, void **addr_ptr, SIZE_T *size
         }
 
         pe_mapping->image.base = wine_server_client_ptr( view->base );
+        /* The view isn't at the address the server assigned when that range
+         * was already in use (on macOS the exe range 0x7ff6..0x7ff8 overlaps
+         * host mappings), and map_image_view() then chose another. Image
+         * information filled from map_addr after this, such as the main
+         * thread's TransferAddress, must use where the image really is. */
+        if (pe_mapping->image.map_addr) pe_mapping->image.map_addr = pe_mapping->image.base;
         SERVER_START_REQ( map_image_view )
         {
             req->mapping = wine_server_obj_handle( mapping );
